From 1db41e639dbb786b1622f5b86a382111a41027d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:38:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] http client: outbounds, the ways a downloader takes in
 the order of what it knows of them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An HTTP client of http_clients may name outbounds instead of a detour: the ways its downloads may
go through, the first one the default first try. The manager gives such a client a downloader
(adapter.HTTPDownloaders): for the host of a file it orders the ways by what it knows — the way
that brought the host's last file, the first of the list, the ways that brought another host's
file (fastest first), those the URL tests passed (lowest delay first), the unknown ones, those
that failed for the host — starts the next way beside those under way when they show no
progress, at most three at once, and takes the first result its caller accepts. What the
downloads found (DownloadMemory) is the manager's, or the one the program that runs the box keeps
in its context. A remote rule-set whose client has outbounds downloads through the downloader; a
body that does not parse fails its way. Users of the client that do not know the downloader go
through the first way.

Pdk-Feature: http-client-downloader
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 04
